<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN SEPTEMBER NEW CAR SALES FALL 2.4 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN SEPTEMBER NEW CAR SALES FALL 2.4 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African new car sales</p>
<p>fell 2.4 percent to 19,928 units in September from 20,420 units</p>
<p>in August and eased 9.5 percent from 22,029 units sold in</p>
<p>September 1995, latest National Association of Automobile</p>
<p>Manufacturers of South Africa figures show.</p>
<p>    Detailed Sales data:	   Sept 96 Aug 96  Sept 95 </p>
<p>    New passenger cars	     19,928  20,420  22,029</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles    10,286  11,038  11,675</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles   502     544     384</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles    638     639     708</p>
<p>    TOTAL:			     31,354  32,641  34,796</p>
<p>Individual manufacturer car sales:</p>
<p>Toyota 8,065, Volkswagen 5,603, Samcor 5,461, Nissan 3,637,</p>
<p>Delta 3,277, Mercedes-Benz 3,147, BMW 1,282, Land Rover SA 402,</p>
<p>Daewoo 168, Iveco 87, Tyco 79, MAN 55, Dacia 42, Erf 21, AAD 10,</p>
<p>Scania 7, Subaru 7, Freightliner 4.</p>
<p>					    Jan-Sept 96   Jan-Sept 95 </p>
<p>    New passenger cars		180,668	 177,623</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles	98,117	  96,969 </p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles	3,933	   3,130</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles	 6,214	   5,759</p>
<p>    TOTAL:				288,932	 283,481</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
